abstract: >-
  Urna is an offline-first vector database that stores text chunks, embeddings,
  source spans, indices, and a search contract in a single .urna file. Python
  tooling builds the file, and a Rust runtime searches it using memory mapping
  and hash verification. Search results include cosine scores and
  content-addressable citations that resolve to stored text and source spans.
  Builds are reproducible for the same inputs and configuration.
